<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Taifa of Santa María del Algarve</h1><p class="st-meta">1018 CE – 1051 CE (approx.) · capital Santa María (Faro)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small taifa at Santa María, today's Faro, ruled by the Arab Banu Harun in the far south of present-day Portugal.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 1018 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/said-ibn-harun">Said ibn Harun</a>, of a local Arab family, made himself independent in the coastal town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faro">Santa María de Harun</a>, the later Faro, and its district in the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algarve">Algarve</a> as caliphal authority disappeared.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The state was a small coastal principality of fishing, salt pans and dry farming, with figs, almonds and olives. Its rulers recognised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammudid-dynasty">Hammudid</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphs</a> for a time and later sought to balance between the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/taifa-of-silves">Taifa of Silves</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a>. Little else is recorded about its government.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 1051 the last ruler, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-said-ibn-harun">Muhammad ibn Said</a>, surrendered his town to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-mutadid-of-seville">al-Mutadid</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/taifa-of-seville">Taifa of Seville</a>. The town's name later gave rise to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faro">Faro</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algarve">Algarve</a> fell to Portugal in 1249.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 1018 CE – 1051 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:79.96%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1018 CE – 1051 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Santa María (Faro)</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Said ibn Harun, Muhammad ibn Said</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Andalusi Arabic, Mozarabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/portugal">Portugal</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Taifa of Faro, Banu Harun</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1034&amp;focus=taifa-of-santa-maria-del-algarve" aria-label="Taifa of Santa María del Algarve on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4508 671 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Taifa of Santa María del Algarve lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4828 927L4850 1088"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4850 1088h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4828 927h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4828 927h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Santa María. <a href="/atlas?year=1034&amp;focus=taifa-of-santa-maria-del-algarve">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

